                     Debugging

--> debugging is a process of finding, understanding and 
    fixing errors or problems in a script.

set -x: debugging mode

--> it displays each command on the terminal before bash executes it.
--> this helps us to understand what command are runnning 
and what values are being passed to them.


set -e: exit when a command fails.

--> set -e tells bash to exit the script when a command fails, in situation
where the option applies.
--> it prevents the script from continuing with the next commandafter an unexpected failure.


